---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const lastUpdated = 'May 7, 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Voxivium"
  description="How Voxivium collects, uses, shares, and protects your information across our website and the Voxivium app."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class="lead">
          Voxivium is built on the principle that civic engagement and personal privacy must
          coexist. This policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the
          choices you have. We've written it in plain English.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="prose">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy covers <strong>voxivium.com</strong> (the website you're reading) and the
          <strong>Voxivium app</strong> (currently in development, planned for U.S. launch). When
          we say "Voxivium," "we," "us," or "our," we mean Voxivium, PBC, a Delaware Public Benefit
          Corporation. When we say "you," we mean a visitor to our website or a user of our app.
        </p>
        <p>
          Voxivium is currently available only to users in the United States. We do not knowingly
          accept signups from outside the U.S.
        </p>

        <h2>The information we collect</h2>

        <h3>From visitors to voxivium.com</h3>
        <p>
          The marketing site collects only what you give us. If you fill out one of our interest
          forms (voter signup, politician inquiry, media or research inquiry, AI lab inquiry), we
          collect the fields you submit—typically your name, email address, and a small set of
          context fields specific to your audience, such as your organization, jurisdiction, or
          intended use case.
        </p>
        <p>
          Beyond that, we use Cloudflare Web Analytics for basic, privacy-respecting traffic
          measurement. Cloudflare Web Analytics does not use cookies and does not fingerprint
          visitors. We do not run Google Analytics, the Meta pixel, or any third-party advertising
          trackers on this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site also stores your color-theme preference (light or dark) in your browser's
          <code>localStorage</code>. That preference never leaves your device.
        </p>

        <h3>From users of the Voxivium app</h3>
        <p>
          Once the app is live, creating a Voxivium voter account involves these categories of
          information:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address and password. Passwords are
            stored as a one-way cryptographic hash—we never see your plaintext password.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Identity verification data.</strong> When you complete identity verification,
            we forward the personal details required by our third-party identity-verification
            provider (such as your full legal name, date of birth, and address) to that provider
            for the sole purpose of confirming who you are. Voxivium does not collect or store
            your government-issued identity documents. We retain only the verification result and
            the facts we need to operate the service (see profile data, below).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Voter registration verification.</strong> We use a third-party
            voter-registration verification service to confirm that you are a U.S. registered
            voter. From that check, we store only your <strong>registration status</strong> and
            your <strong>assigned voter districts</strong> (federal, state, and local). We do not
            collect or store your voting history.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Profile data.</strong> Your real first name and last name, residential
            address, date of birth, political party affiliation, gender, voter districts, and—only
            if you choose to provide it—your race or ethnicity.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Civic input.</strong> Your stated stances and importance ratings on beliefs,
            your responses to polls, and your stances on specific pieces of legislation, executive
            orders, and court rulings.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Payment information.</strong> If you subscribe to a premium tier, payment
            details are processed by our third-party payment processor. Voxivium does not store
            full payment-card numbers; we receive only the limited transaction metadata required
            to manage your subscription.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical data.</strong> Device type, operating system, app version, IP
            address, and similar diagnostic information used to deliver the service securely.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Notification preferences.</strong> Your settings for push, email, and in-app
            notifications.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>To run the service.</strong> Generating your personal report cards, candidate
            comparisons, polling experiences, and notifications all require the data above.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To keep your records current.</strong> We periodically re-check your voter
            registration status (typically quarterly) so that your assigned representatives and
            districts stay accurate, and to detect changes such as a move or a registration lapse.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To produce aggregated, anonymized insights.</strong> The civic data you
            provide is the foundation of the aggregated, anonymized statistics we share with paid
            customers (politicians, media, researchers, AI labs)—described below.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To communicate with you.</strong> Service announcements, security alerts, and
            notifications you've opted into.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To improve and secure the service.</strong> Diagnostic data, abuse detection,
            and standard product analytics.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>To comply with the law.</strong> Where we are legally required to retain or
            disclose information.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we share your information</h2>

        <h3>What we will never sell or share</h3>
        <p>
          Voxivium will <strong
            >never sell or share your personally identifiable information</strong
          >, including your name, residential address, date of birth, email address, or phone
          number. That commitment is part of the platform's design and is reflected in our
          corporate bylaws.
        </p>

        <h3>What we may share, only as aggregated and anonymized data</h3>
        <p>
          The whole purpose of Voxivium is to translate civic input into a clear collective
          signal. To paid customers (politicians, media organizations, academic researchers, and
          AI labs), we may share <strong>aggregated, anonymized</strong> data derived from the
          following categories:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Political party affiliation</li>
          <li>Gender</li>
          <li>Race or ethnicity (only where you have voluntarily provided it)</li>
          <li>Belief stances and importance ratings</li>
          <li>Polling responses</li>
          <li>Stances on specific issues, legislation, court rulings, and executive orders</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          "Aggregated and anonymized" means these data are reported only as group statistics
          scoped to a geographic area or demographic segment—never as individual records and never
          tied to your identity. We apply minimum-group-size thresholds and other safeguards to
          prevent re-identification.
        </p>

        <h3>Service providers</h3>
        <p>
          We rely on a small set of vetted third parties to operate the service. Each is bound by
          contract to use your data only as we direct:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Identity verification:</strong> [IDV PROVIDER]</li>
          <li><strong>Voter registration verification:</strong> [VRV PROVIDER]</li>
          <li><strong>Hosting and content delivery:</strong> Cloudflare</li>
          <li><strong>Web analytics:</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics</li>
          <li><strong>Payments:</strong> [PAYMENT PROCESSOR]</li>
          <li><strong>Email delivery:</strong> our transactional email provider</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Legal disclosures</h3>
        <p>
          We may disclose information when we are legally required to do so—for example, in
          response to a valid subpoena, court order, or other lawful government request. We will
          challenge requests we believe to be overbroad or unlawful, and where we are not legally
          prohibited from doing so, we will notify the affected user before complying.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>
          The marketing site does not set tracking cookies. Cloudflare Web Analytics, our
          analytics provider, is cookie-free by design. We use your browser's <code
            >localStorage</code
          > only to remember your color-theme preference, which is not a tracking technology.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Voxivium app uses standard, essential session technologies to keep you signed in.
          These are not used for cross-context advertising or third-party tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Access and correction.</strong> You can view and update your profile data from
            within your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Deletion.</strong> You can delete your Voxivium account, and the data
            associated with it, at any time from within the app. Deletion timelines are described
            under "Data retention," below.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Communication preferences.</strong> You can change which notifications you
            receive at any time. Transactional messages required to operate your account
            (security alerts, billing notices) cannot be disabled while your account remains
            active.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>California residents.</strong> California law gives you specific rights to
            know, access, correct, delete, and limit the use of your personal information, and
            the right not to be discriminated against for exercising those rights. To exercise any
            of these rights, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com"
              >privacy@voxivium.com</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Other U.S. state residents.</strong> Several states grant similar rights. We
            extend the substance of those rights to all U.S. users on request. Contact <a
              href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
            >.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain your account data for as long as your account is active. When you delete your
          account—or when we delete it for one of the reasons described below—your data is
          removed from our production systems within <strong>30 days</strong> and is purged from
          encrypted backups within <strong>90 days</strong>. After deletion, only the
          aggregated, anonymized signal you contributed remains; that signal cannot be
          reconstructed back to you.
        </p>
        <p>We may delete an account, with or without notice, in the following cases:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The user signs up but does not complete identity verification within a reasonable
            window.
          </li>
          <li>
            The user completes identity verification and is determined to be under 18 years of
            age.
          </li>
          <li>
            The account is dormant or inactive for an extended period, as described in our Terms.
          </li>
          <li>The account is found to be fraudulent or in material breach of our Terms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may retain limited information for longer where required by law (for example, tax,
          accounting, or fraud-prevention obligations).
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          We protect your information with industry-standard safeguards: encryption in transit
          (TLS) and at rest, scoped access controls, audit logging, and regular security reviews.
          No system is perfectly secure, and we will not promise otherwise—but we will treat your
          data with the care that civic trust requires.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Voxivium is intended for U.S. registered voters and is not directed to anyone under 18.
          We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe
          a child has provided us with personal information, contact <a
            href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a
          > and we will promptly delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>International users</h2>
        <p>
          Voxivium currently operates only in the United States. Our servers and service
          providers are located in the United States. If you are located outside the U.S., please
          do not use the Voxivium app.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last
          updated" date above and, for material changes, give you advance notice through the
          service or by email. Your continued use of Voxivium after a change takes effect means
          you accept the updated policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, requests to exercise your rights, or any other privacy-related
          inquiries:
        </p>
        <p class="contact">
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="mailto:privacy@voxivium.com">privacy@voxivium.com</a><br />
          <strong>Mail:</strong><br />
          Voxivium, PBC<br />
          921 Pleasant Valley Ave #561<br />
          Mount Laurel, NJ 08054
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

